  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "26",
  "quote": "A landlord may enter a rental unit at any time without written notice, (a) in cases of emergency; or (b) if the tenant consents to the entry at the time of entry.",
  "reason": "Section 25 states a landlord may enter a unit only in accordance with sections 26 or 27, and section 26(1)(b) requires that consent to enter without notice be given at the time of entry, not in advance in the tenancy agreement. Because the clause is inconsistent with these entry rules, it is void under section 4(1)."
}

